{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-85528232-773b-4a2e-983c-50a201c03756","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-98a1405bf5a038d2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-ilysfpfr/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md","content":"# AMD Instinct validation campaign for vLLM ROCm serving\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic runs the validation campaign that establishes first-hand functional\nand performance parity data for vLLM serving of the platform's supported model\nset on physical AMD Instinct accelerators, and produces the go/no-go scope for\nproductization. It resolves the strategy's central unknown — whether upstream\nvLLM ROCm builds deliver acceptable parity for our supported models — which\ndetermines the scope of the serving runtime productization work.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Stand up the validation environment on dedicated AMD Instinct nodes\n  (procured or partner-lab access — see Risks), including the ROCm driver and\n  runtime stack and the upstream vLLM ROCm builds.\n- Execute a functional validation pass: serve each model in the supported\n  model set under vLLM on ROCm, exercised through a KServe InferenceService\n  (raw deployment or serverless mode), recording pass/fail per model.\n- Execute a performance validation pass: measure serving throughput and\n  latency per model on the AMD Instinct hardware against the CUDA baseline on\n  comparable hardware.\n- Produce the campaign report: per-model functional results, performance\n  parity data, observed driver/runtime prerequisites, and a per-model go/no-go\n  recommendation that defines the productization scope.\n- Validate that KServe lifecycle and routing work unchanged on AMD GPU nodes\n  (KServe requires no code changes; this confirmation is part of the campaign).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Every model in the supported model set has a recorded functional\n  pass/fail result for vLLM serving on ROCm, exercised through a KServe\n  InferenceService.\n- Every functionally-passing model has recorded throughput and latency\n  measurements on AMD Instinct hardware, alongside the CUDA baseline\n  measurements used for comparison.\n- The campaign report delivers a per-model go/no-go recommendation that\n  defines which models proceed to productization.\n- The driver and runtime prerequisites observed on the AMD nodes are\n  documented in the campaign report.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)**: A validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware\n  establishes functional and performance parity data for vLLM serving of the\n  supported model set, producing the go/no-go scope for productization. This\n  epic is the entirety of HLR-1.\n\n## Risks\n\n- **Hardware access is an availability precondition outside this strategy's\n  control**: dedicated AMD Instinct nodes do not exist in the CI fleet, and\n  procurement or partner-lab access is unresolved. This epic's work includes\n  securing access, but the access being granted is not a condition the epic's\n  deliverable produces — the campaign timeline depends on it.\n- Upstream vLLM ROCm image releases are controlled by AMD and the upstream\n  communities; the campaign pins available upstream builds and is not gated on\n  release-train alignment.\n- Re-split trigger: if the supported-model matrix exceeds a single campaign\n  window, split into staged per-model-family campaign epics.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44299,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad1452d411d62271","agent_id":"af035a9c6d4afd483","session_id":"ee31f95d-bee0-49c9-bebd-617d8f30fd03","uuid":"8d9b501e-050b-4a02-8036-77b174abbe59","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:09:07.245Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
