{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-85528232-773b-4a2e-983c-50a201c03756","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b57a159ffa9bb60e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-ilysfpfr/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E002.md","content":"# Upstream ROCm image cadence assessment and base-image strategy\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic resolves the strategy's open question about upstream ROCm build\ncadence: whether AMD's runtime image releases and the upstream communities'\nROCm builds (vLLM serving images and PyTorch training images) align with the\nplatform's release trains. Its deliverable is a base-image strategy for all\nproductized ROCm runtimes — pin upstream images where cadence aligns, or build\nfrom source with carried patches where it does not — which determines the\napproach of the serving runtime productization and the PyTorch training\nsupport work.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Collect the release history and cadence of AMD ROCm runtime releases and\n  upstream vLLM / PyTorch ROCm image publications from public release records.\n- Map that cadence against the platform's release train dates and support\n  windows.\n- Produce the base-image strategy: for each productized ROCm runtime (vLLM\n  serving runtime, PyTorch training worker images), whether to pin an upstream\n  image or build from source with patches, including the pinning and upgrade\n  criteria.\n- Record the misalignment scenarios and their mitigations (e.g. carrying\n  patches, building from source, deferring a runtime to a later train) so the\n  downstream implementation epics have a defined fallback.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A documented cadence analysis maps AMD ROCm and upstream vLLM/PyTorch ROCm\n  image release history against platform release train dates.\n- A base-image strategy exists for each productized ROCm runtime, stating pin\n  vs build-from-source with explicit selection criteria.\n- Each misalignment scenario identified by the analysis carries a recorded\n  mitigation that the downstream implementation epics can apply without\n  re-opening the assessment.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P0)**: enables the productization of a supported vLLM ROCm serving\n  runtime by selecting its base-image strategy (gating input, not direct\n  scope).\n- **HLR-3 (P1)**: enables PyTorch training on ROCm by selecting the PyTorch\n  ROCm worker-image strategy (gating input, not direct scope).\n\n## Risks\n\n- AMD's release cadence is outside our control; the assessment documents and\n  plans around it rather than changing it. If cadence fundamentally cannot\n  support release trains, the fallback is the build-from-source strategy this\n  epic selects.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44299,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad1452d411d62271","agent_id":"af035a9c6d4afd483","session_id":"ee31f95d-bee0-49c9-bebd-617d8f30fd03","uuid":"a9d5a49e-378c-4d8a-9def-622013a9e4ce","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:09:13.724Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
