y selected by the cadence assessment.\n- Serving of each cleared model is verified on AMD Instinct hardware through\n  a KServe InferenceService.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P0)**: A supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for\n  the models the validation campaign clears. This epic is the entirety of\n  HLR-2's productization scope (the build pipeline work is tracked separately\n  as an enabler).\n\n## Risks\n\n- Scope is bounded by the validation campaign's go/no-go outcome: if the\n  campaign clears a smaller model set than the supported set, productization\n  covers only the cleared models; if it clears none, productization is\n  descoped to a future release and hardware access is revisited.\n- Upstream ROCm image cadence is controlled by AMD; if it misaligns with\n  release trains, the fallback is the build-from-source strategy selected by\n  the cadence assessment.\n- Re-split trigger: split by model family if per-model bring-up exceeds the\n  estimated volume and the epic outgrows a sprint.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47078,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad1452d411d62271","agent_id":"af035a9c6d4afd483","session_id":"ee31f95d-bee0-49c9-bebd-617d8f30fd03","uuid":"8e714c22-3fc6-4323-bf76-650803ea3b3b","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:09:32.422Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
