{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-dc452421-73a1-4981-86cb-2bc870da2dcf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-89348902c2a9bbb1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-ilysfpfr/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E005.md","content":"# Kueue quota handling for amd.com/gpu\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic adds amd.com/gpu quota handling to the platform's queueing layer so\nthat workloads requesting AMD GPUs are admitted with correct quota accounting.\nIt extends the existing ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model — already proven\nfor NVIDIA GPU resources — to the AMD GPU resource name, including gang\n(all-or-nothing) admission semantics for multi-GPU jobs.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define Kueue resource flavors and quota configuration covering\n  amd.com/gpu (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue coverage for AMD GPU nodes), mirroring\n  the existing NVIDIA GPU quota handling.\n- Ensure all-or-nothing admission (waitForPodsReady gang semantics) applies\n  correctly to workloads requesting amd.com/gpu, including multi-GPU jobs.\n- Verify queueing behavior — pending/admitted workload accounting and quota\n  enforcement — for amd.com/gpu workloads.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Kueue quota configuration supports amd.com/gpu: a workload requesting\n  amd.com/gpu is admitted against the correct quota and queue accounting is\n  exposed as before.\n- All-or-nothing admission is verified for multi-GPU jobs requesting\n  amd.com/gpu (a job is admitted only when its full GPU allocation can be\n  satisfied).\n- Quota enforcement is demonstrated: a workload exceeding the configured\n  amd.com/gpu quota remains pending rather than partially admitted.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3 (P1)**: PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and\n  multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling.\n  This epic delivers the quota-handling half; the Training Operator job\n  support is tracked separately (same HLR, different component).\n\n## Risks\n\n- Full end-to-end admission demonstration with running AMD GPU pods benefits\n  from AMD Instinct nodes; quota accounting and admission semantics can be\n  validated against the resource flavor configuration without them.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47078,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad1452d411d62271","agent_id":"af035a9c6d4afd483","session_id":"ee31f95d-bee0-49c9-bebd-617d8f30fd03","uuid":"cf574ac2-c77b-4bce-a18f-55c1397185e0","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:09:44.293Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
