{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b2770027-f7b1-4060-9d70-a0a6b28bdfee","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaa0236b1e267b59","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-ilysfpfr/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E006.md","content":"# PyTorch ROCm training support with Training Operator\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic makes PyTorch training on ROCm a supported path for single- and\nmulti-GPU jobs run through the Training Operator, using PyTorch ROCm worker\nimages selected by the upstream cadence assessment's base-image strategy. It\nextends the existing accelerated-training support — already proven for NVIDIA\nGPUs — to AMD Instinct accelerators, with jobs admitted through the platform's\nqueueing layer using amd.com/gpu quota.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Support PyTorchJob single-GPU and multi-GPU (distributed) training jobs on\n  ROCm: worker pods scheduled onto AMD GPU nodes requesting amd.com/gpu.\n- Provide/select the PyTorch ROCm worker image per the base-image strategy\n  chosen by the upstream ROCm cadence assessment (pinned upstream image or\n  build-from-source with patches).\n- Verify job admission through Kueue for amd.com/gpu workloads, including\n  multi-GPU gang admission (the quota configuration itself is tracked as\n  separate queueing-layer work; this epic verifies the end-to-end training\n  path against it).\n- Establish the supported status for the ROCm training path (single- and\n  multi-GPU).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A single-GPU PyTorchJob requesting amd.com/gpu runs to completion on AMD\n  Instinct worker nodes with the selected PyTorch ROCm worker image.\n- A multi-GPU (distributed) PyTorchJob requesting amd.com/gpu runs to\n  completion on AMD Instinct worker nodes.\n- Multi-GPU jobs are admitted through Kueue with all-or-nothing semantics\n  against amd.com/gpu quota.\n- The PyTorch ROCm worker image strategy applied (pinned or built) matches the\n  base-image strategy selected by the cadence assessment.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3 (P1)**: PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and\n  multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling.\n  This epic delivers the Training Operator job-support half; the Kueue quota\n  handling is tracked separately (same HLR, different component).\n\n## Risks\n\n- Validation on physical AMD Instinct nodes depends on hardware access\n  (procurement or partner-lab), which is an availability precondition outside\n  this strategy's control — recorded here rather than as an acceptance\n  criterion; the ACs above sit on the demonstrated training jobs.\n- Upstream PyTorch ROCm image cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream\n  communities; if it misaligns with release trains, the fallback is the\n  build-from-source strategy selected by the cadence assessment.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":51193,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad1452d411d62271","agent_id":"af035a9c6d4afd483","session_id":"ee31f95d-bee0-49c9-bebd-617d8f30fd03","uuid":"9b0889c1-4e69-4bf2-a06d-1cc046538cc4","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:10:05.934Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
