{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b226f75742b0fab8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9020\n3\ttitle: AMD GPU (ROCm) enablement for serving and training\n4\tstatus: Refinement Done\n5\tpriority: Major\n6\tlabels:\n7\t- refined\n8\t- hardware\n9\tlinks: []\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t## Problem Statement\n13\t\n14\tTwo strategic customers are standardizing on AMD Instinct accelerators and need\n15\tRHOAI to serve and train on ROCm. Upstream vLLM and PyTorch both publish ROCm\n16\tsupport, but the platform ships only CUDA runtime builds, and we have no\n17\tfirst-hand data on functional or performance parity for our supported model\n18\tset. Feature and performance validation requires physical AMD GPU hardware —\n19\tnone exists in our CI fleet today — and upstream ROCm image cadence is\n20\tcontrolled by AMD and the upstream communities.\n21\t\n22\t## High-Level Requirements\n23\t\n24\t| ID | Priority | Requirement |\n25\t|-------|----------|-------------|\n26\t| HLR-1 | P0 | A validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware establishes functional and performance parity data for vLLM serving of the supported model set, producing the go/no-go scope for productization. |\n27\t| HLR-2 | P0 | A supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the models the validation campaign clears. |\n28\t| HLR-3 | P1 | PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling. |\n29\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, and the validated model list. |\n30\t\n31\t## Affected Components\n32\t\n33\t- KServe\n34\t- Serving Runtimes\n35\t- Training Operator\n36\t- Distributed Workloads\n37\t\n38\t## Out of Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Intel Gaudi or other non-AMD accelerator families\n41\t- AMD GPU sharing/partitioning support\n42\t\n43\t## Open Questions\n44\t\n45\t1. Hardware access: the validation campaign (HLR-1) needs dedicated AMD\n46\t   Instinct nodes — procurement or partner-lab access is unresolved.\n47\t2. Upstream ROCm build cadence: whether AMD's runtime image releases align\n48\t   with our release trains is outside our control.\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-adab5e6321da8d4c","agent_id":"a6effe46579c22326","session_id":"ee31f95d-bee0-49c9-bebd-617d8f30fd03","uuid":"5301734a-c356-4433-9623-6b9adf0561b9","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:11:42.787Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b226f75742b0fab8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
