{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-affc732fba9a1590","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n3\ttitle: AMD Instinct validation campaign for vLLM ROCm serving\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -2\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# AMD Instinct validation campaign for vLLM ROCm serving\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis epic runs the validation campaign that establishes first-hand functional\n30\tand performance parity data for vLLM serving of the platform's supported model\n31\tset on physical AMD Instinct accelerators, and produces the go/no-go scope for\n32\tproductization. It resolves the strategy's central unknown — whether upstream\n33\tvLLM ROCm builds deliver acceptable parity for our supported models — which\n34\tdetermines the scope of the serving runtime productization work.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Stand up the validation environment on dedicated AMD Instinct nodes\n39\t  (procured or partner-lab access — see Risks), including the ROCm driver and\n40\t  runtime stack and the upstream vLLM ROCm builds.\n41\t- Execute a functional validation pass: serve each model in the supported\n42\t  model set under vLLM on ROCm, exercised through a KServe InferenceService\n43\t  (raw deployment or serverless mode), recording pass/fail per model.\n44\t- Execute a performance validation pass: measure serving throughput and\n45\t  latency per model on the AMD Instinct hardware against the CUDA baseline on\n46\t  comparable hardware.\n47\t- Produce the campaign report: per-model functional results, performance\n48\t  parity data, observed driver/runtime prerequisites, and a per-model go/no-go\n49\t  recommendation that defines the productization scope.\n50\t- Validate that KServe lifecycle and routing work unchanged on AMD GPU nodes\n51\t  (KServe requires no code changes; this confirmation is part of the campaign).\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- Every model in the supported model set has a recorded functional\n56\t  pass/fail result for vLLM serving on ROCm, exercised through a KServe\n57\t  InferenceService.\n58\t- Every functionally-passing model has recorded throughput and latency\n59\t  measurements on AMD Instinct hardware, alongside the CUDA baseline\n60\t  measurements used for comparison.\n61\t- The campaign report delivers a per-model go/no-go recommendation that\n62\t  defines which models proceed to productization.\n63\t- The driver and runtime prerequisites observed on the AMD nodes are\n64\t  documented in the campaign report.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: A validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware\n69\t  establishes functional and performance parity data for vLLM serving of the\n70\t  supported model set, producing the go/no-go scope for productization. This\n71\t  epic is the entirety of HLR-1.\n72\t\n73\t## Risks\n74\t\n75\t- **Hardware access is an availability precondition outside this strategy's\n76\t  control**: dedicated AMD Instinct nodes do not exist in the CI fleet, and\n77\t  procurement or partner-lab access is unresolved. This epic's work includes\n78\t  securing access, but the access being granted is not a condition the epic's\n79\t  deliverable produces — the campaign timeline depends on it.\n80\t- Upstream vLLM ROCm image releases are controlled by AMD and the upstream\n81\t  communities; the campaign pins available upstream builds and is not gated on\n82\t  release-train alignment.\n83\t- Re-split trigger: if the supported-model matrix exceeds a single campaign\n84\t  window, split into staged per-model-family campaign epics.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-adab5e6321da8d4c","agent_id":"a6effe46579c22326","session_id":"ee31f95d-bee0-49c9-bebd-617d8f30fd03","uuid":"7d2c5d80-a8f4-4947-83ef-bad6aa964fe4","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:11:46.842Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-affc732fba9a1590","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
