{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9145fe2467952e2f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E003\n3\ttitle: Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: Productize only the model set the validation campaign clears;\n16\t    if the campaign clears none, descope productization to a future release and revisit\n17\t    hardware access.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: -1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic productizes a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for the model set\n40\tthe AMD Instinct validation campaign clears. It takes the vLLM ROCm build in\n41\tthe existing midstream repository from an upstream-only capability to a\n42\tproductized, supported runtime shipped for the platform, applying the\n43\tbase-image strategy selected by the upstream ROCm cadence assessment.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Build the vLLM ROCm serving runtime image in the existing midstream vLLM\n48\t  repository, per the base-image strategy (pinned upstream ROCm base or\n49\t  build-from-source with patches).\n50\t- Productize the runtime as a supported serving runtime for the cleared model\n51\t  set (runtime distribution and support status — the platform currently ships\n52\t  only CUDA builds; ROCm builds exist upstream but are not shipped or\n53\t  supported).\n54\t- Verify serving of each cleared model on AMD Instinct hardware through a\n55\t  KServe InferenceService as part of bring-up.\n56\t- Wire the image build through the midstream Konflux pipeline (the pipeline\n57\t  onboarding work for the ROCm image variant runs in parallel — the coupling\n58\t  is enforced by the build-pipeline acceptance criterion below, not by a\n59\t  scheduling dependency).\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- A vLLM ROCm serving runtime image builds in the midstream repository for\n64\t  the model set cleared by the validation campaign.\n65\t- The ROCm image variant builds green in the midstream Konflux pipeline\n66\t  (build pipeline green).\n67\t- The runtime is productized with supported status for the cleared model set,\n68\t  applying the base-image strategy selected by the cadence assessment.\n69\t- Serving of each cleared model is verified on AMD Instinct hardware through\n70\t  a KServe InferenceService.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- **HLR-2 (P0)**: A supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for\n75\t  the models the validation campaign clears. This epic is the entirety of\n76\t  HLR-2's productization scope (the build pipeline work is tracked separately\n77\t  as an enabler).\n78\t\n79\t## Risks\n80\t\n81\t- Scope is bounded by the validation campaign's go/no-go outcome: if the\n82\t  campaign clears a smaller model set than the supported set, productization\n83\t  covers only the cleared models; if it clears none, productization is\n84\t  descoped to a future release and hardware access is revisited.\n85\t- Upstream ROCm image cadence is controlled by AMD; if it misaligns with\n86\t  release trains, the fallback is the build-from-source strategy selected by\n87\t  the cadence assessment.\n88\t- Re-split trigger: split by model family if per-model bring-up exceeds the\n89\t  estimated volume and the epic outgrows a sprint.\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d5f34aa3bcc6919","agent_id":"ab100ec37a64d7cbd","session_id":"ee31f95d-bee0-49c9-bebd-617d8f30fd03","uuid":"f3917649-96c1-4c62-becc-f9fa2bd31205","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:16:04.403Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9145fe2467952e2f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
