{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-945dbe9798272fe8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n3\ttitle: Upstream ROCm image cadence assessment and base-image strategy\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Upstream ROCm image cadence assessment and base-image strategy\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis epic resolves the strategy's open question about upstream ROCm build\n30\tcadence: whether AMD's runtime image releases and the upstream communities'\n31\tROCm builds (vLLM serving images and PyTorch training images) align with the\n32\tplatform's release trains. Its deliverable is a base-image strategy for all\n33\tproductized ROCm runtimes — pin upstream images where cadence aligns, or build\n34\tfrom source with carried patches where it does not — which determines the\n35\tapproach of the serving runtime productization and the PyTorch training\n36\tsupport work.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Collect the release history and cadence of AMD ROCm runtime releases and\n41\t  upstream vLLM / PyTorch ROCm image publications from public release records.\n42\t- Map that cadence against the platform's release train dates and support\n43\t  windows.\n44\t- Produce the base-image strategy: for each productized ROCm runtime (vLLM\n45\t  serving runtime, PyTorch training worker images), whether to pin an upstream\n46\t  image or build from source with patches, including the pinning and upgrade\n47\t  criteria.\n48\t- Record the misalignment scenarios and their mitigations (e.g. carrying\n49\t  patches, building from source, deferring a runtime to a later train) so the\n50\t  downstream implementation epics have a defined fallback.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- A documented cadence analysis maps AMD ROCm and upstream vLLM/PyTorch ROCm\n55\t  image release history against platform release train dates.\n56\t- A base-image strategy exists for each productized ROCm runtime, stating pin\n57\t  vs build-from-source with explicit selection criteria.\n58\t- Each misalignment scenario identified by the analysis carries a recorded\n59\t  mitigation that the downstream implementation epics can apply without\n60\t  re-opening the assessment.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- **HLR-2 (P0)**: enables the productization of a supported vLLM ROCm serving\n65\t  runtime by selecting its base-image strategy (gating input, not direct\n66\t  scope).\n67\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: enables PyTorch training on ROCm by selecting the PyTorch\n68\t  ROCm worker-image strategy (gating input, not direct scope).\n69\t\n70\t## Risks\n71\t\n72\t- AMD's release cadence is outside our control; the assessment documents and\n73\t  plans around it rather than changing it. If cadence fundamentally cannot\n74\t  support release trains, the fallback is the build-from-source strategy this\n75\t  epic selects.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2a98fe0ecec4dd8","agent_id":"a984887860b9faab1","session_id":"ee31f95d-bee0-49c9-bebd-617d8f30fd03","uuid":"c5cea8db-55f7-4ee3-bbf4-3828e716afc2","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:17:17.446Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-945dbe9798272fe8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
