{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8e58cea893c2316","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E003\n3\ttitle: Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: Productize only the model set the validation campaign clears;\n16\t    if the campaign clears none, descope productization to a future release and revisit\n17\t    hardware access. If the cadence assessment instead selects build-from-source (upstream\n18\t    ROCm image cadence misaligns with release trains), apply that base-image strategy\n19\t    here — the productization approach changes, not its scope.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 1\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: 0\n26\t  external_dependency: -1\n27\t  human_process_gates: 0\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 4\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\tbranch: null\n36\t---\n37\t# Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tThis epic productizes a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for the model set\n42\tthe AMD Instinct validation campaign clears. It takes the vLLM ROCm build in\n43\tthe existing midstream repository from an upstream-only capability to a\n44\tproductized, supported runtime shipped for the platform, applying the\n45\tbase-image strategy selected by the upstream ROCm cadence assessment.\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\t- Build the vLLM ROCm serving runtime image in the existing midstream vLLM\n50\t  repository, per the base-image strategy (pinned upstream ROCm base or\n51\t  build-from-source with patches).\n52\t- Productize the runtime as a supported serving runtime for the cleared model\n53\t  set (runtime distribution and support status — the platform currently ships\n54\t  only CUDA builds; ROCm builds exist upstream but are not shipped or\n55\t  supported).\n56\t- Verify serving of each cleared model on AMD Instinct hardware through a\n57\t  KServe InferenceService as part of bring-up.\n58\t- Wire the image build through the midstream Konflux pipeline (the pipeline\n59\t  onboarding work for the ROCm image variant runs in parallel — the coupling\n60\t  is enforced by the build-pipeline acceptance criterion below, not by a\n61\t  scheduling dependency).\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- A vLLM ROCm serving runtime image builds in the midstream repository for\n66\t  the model set cleared by the validation campaign.\n67\t- The ROCm image variant builds green in the midstream Konflux pipeline\n68\t  (build pipeline green).\n69\t- The runtime is productized with supported status for the cleared model set,\n70\t  applying the base-image strategy selected by the cadence assessment.\n71\t- Serving of each cleared model is verified on AMD Instinct hardware through\n72\t  a KServe InferenceService.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- **HLR-2 (P0)**: A supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for\n77\t  the models the validation campaign clears. This epic is the entirety of\n78\t  HLR-2's productization scope (the build pipeline work is tracked separately\n79\t  as an enabler).\n80\t\n81\t## Risks\n82\t\n83\t- Scope is bounded by the validation campaign's go/no-go outcome: if the\n84\t  campaign clears a smaller model set than the supported set, productization\n85\t  covers only the cleared models; if it clears none, productization is\n86\t  descoped to a future release and hardware access is revisited.\n87\t- Upstream ROCm image cadence is controlled by AMD; if it misaligns with\n88\t  release trains, the fallback is the build-from-source strategy selected by\n89\t  the cadence assessment.\n90\t- Re-split trigger: split by model family if per-model bring-up exceeds the\n91\t  estimated volume and the epic outgrows a sprint.\n92\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2a98fe0ecec4dd8","agent_id":"a984887860b9faab1","session_id":"ee31f95d-bee0-49c9-bebd-617d8f30fd03","uuid":"9fc50a27-3deb-4ac5-a4e1-c5fbf27db06c","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:17:20.885Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8e58cea893c2316","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
