{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d19c125cb220abd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E005\n3\ttitle: Kueue quota handling for amd.com/gpu\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue quota handling for amd.com/gpu\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic adds amd.com/gpu quota handling to the platform's queueing layer so\n34\tthat workloads requesting AMD GPUs are admitted with correct quota accounting.\n35\tIt extends the existing ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model — already proven\n36\tfor NVIDIA GPU resources — to the AMD GPU resource name, including gang\n37\t(all-or-nothing) admission semantics for multi-GPU jobs.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Define Kueue resource flavors and quota configuration covering\n42\t  amd.com/gpu (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue coverage for AMD GPU nodes), mirroring\n43\t  the existing NVIDIA GPU quota handling.\n44\t- Ensure all-or-nothing admission (waitForPodsReady gang semantics) applies\n45\t  correctly to workloads requesting amd.com/gpu, including multi-GPU jobs.\n46\t- Verify queueing behavior — pending/admitted workload accounting and quota\n47\t  enforcement — for amd.com/gpu workloads.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Kueue quota configuration supports amd.com/gpu: a workload requesting\n52\t  amd.com/gpu is admitted against the correct quota and queue accounting is\n53\t  exposed as before.\n54\t- All-or-nothing admission is verified for multi-GPU jobs requesting\n55\t  amd.com/gpu (a job is admitted only when its full GPU allocation can be\n56\t  satisfied).\n57\t- Quota enforcement is demonstrated: a workload exceeding the configured\n58\t  amd.com/gpu quota remains pending rather than partially admitted.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and\n63\t  multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling.\n64\t  This epic delivers the quota-handling half; the Training Operator job\n65\t  support is tracked separately (same HLR, different component).\n66\t\n67\t## Risks\n68\t\n69\t- Full end-to-end admission demonstration with running AMD GPU pods benefits\n70\t  from AMD Instinct nodes; quota accounting and admission semantics can be\n71\t  validated against the resource flavor configuration without them.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2a98fe0ecec4dd8","agent_id":"a984887860b9faab1","session_id":"ee31f95d-bee0-49c9-bebd-617d8f30fd03","uuid":"dc4a7a2e-e12b-437b-8937-42c7e70c776f","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:17:24.494Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d19c125cb220abd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
