{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9253e6384ef223df","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E006\n3\ttitle: PyTorch ROCm training support with Training Operator\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Training Operator\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If upstream ROCm image cadence does not align with release trains,\n15\t    apply the build-from-source worker image strategy the cadence assessment selects,\n16\t    or defer the multi-GPU validation window.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: 0\n23\t  external_dependency: -1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 4\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# PyTorch ROCm training support with Training Operator\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic makes PyTorch training on ROCm a supported path for single- and\n39\tmulti-GPU jobs run through the Training Operator, using PyTorch ROCm worker\n40\timages selected by the upstream cadence assessment's base-image strategy. It\n41\textends the existing accelerated-training support — already proven for NVIDIA\n42\tGPUs — to AMD Instinct accelerators, with jobs admitted through the platform's\n43\tqueueing layer using amd.com/gpu quota.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Support PyTorchJob single-GPU and multi-GPU (distributed) training jobs on\n48\t  ROCm: worker pods scheduled onto AMD GPU nodes requesting amd.com/gpu.\n49\t- Provide/select the PyTorch ROCm worker image per the base-image strategy\n50\t  chosen by the upstream ROCm cadence assessment (pinned upstream image or\n51\t  build-from-source with patches).\n52\t- Verify job admission through Kueue for amd.com/gpu workloads, including\n53\t  multi-GPU gang admission (the quota configuration itself is tracked as\n54\t  separate queueing-layer work; this epic verifies the end-to-end training\n55\t  path against it).\n56\t- Establish the supported status for the ROCm training path (single- and\n57\t  multi-GPU).\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- A single-GPU PyTorchJob requesting amd.com/gpu runs to completion on AMD\n62\t  Instinct worker nodes with the selected PyTorch ROCm worker image.\n63\t- A multi-GPU (distributed) PyTorchJob requesting amd.com/gpu runs to\n64\t  completion on AMD Instinct worker nodes.\n65\t- Multi-GPU jobs are admitted through Kueue with all-or-nothing semantics\n66\t  against amd.com/gpu quota.\n67\t- The PyTorch ROCm worker image strategy applied (pinned or built) matches the\n68\t  base-image strategy selected by the cadence assessment.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and\n73\t  multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling.\n74\t  This epic delivers the Training Operator job-support half; the Kueue quota\n75\t  handling is tracked separately (same HLR, different component).\n76\t\n77\t## Risks\n78\t\n79\t- Validation on physical AMD Instinct nodes depends on hardware access\n80\t  (procurement or partner-lab), which is an availability precondition outside\n81\t  this strategy's control — recorded here rather than as an acceptance\n82\t  criterion; the ACs above sit on the demonstrated training jobs.\n83\t- Upstream PyTorch ROCm image cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream\n84\t  communities; if it misaligns with release trains, the fallback is the\n85\t  build-from-source strategy selected by the cadence assessment.\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2a98fe0ecec4dd8","agent_id":"a984887860b9faab1","session_id":"ee31f95d-bee0-49c9-bebd-617d8f30fd03","uuid":"f67d5500-bdfe-4998-b869-513eee7712e5","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:17:25.096Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9253e6384ef223df","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
