rline call. I'd call it arguable → Criterion 5 = 1? Or accept the decomposer's distinction?\n\nHmm. Let me think about the semantics more carefully. The 9-signal rubric presumably scores -1/0/+1. For open_questions: +1 all resolved, -1 unresolved questions that change approach, 0 = in between (some questions, mitigated/resolved by gating). E003's situation: open questions exist at strategy time, resolved by gates before epic start. That's precisely the \"in between\" case — the epic isn't independent of open questions (unlike E005), but they're structured away. 0 seems defensible, even well-calibrated. E006 similarly: open_questions 0, \"resolved by the gating cadence assessment before this epic starts\". Consistent treatment between E003 and E006. E005 (+1, no open questions affect it) and E007 (+1, all structural decisions resolved) are the genuinely-independent cases. So the decomposer applies a consistent, defensible calibration: gated questions → 0, no questions → +1. I find this coherent. Criterion 5 = 2.\n\nNow architecture_claims: E003/E004/E005/E006 = +1 with cited files — verified correct above. E007 = 0 with \"no context file for Documentation\" — correct (no Documentation file in .context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/). But wait — the calibration check: \"a strategy makes architecture claims whenever it states what a component IS... When the strategy's premise asserts such a state and an architecture-context file covers the component, an epic shaped by that premise that scores architecture_claims: 0 ... is a calibration miss\". E007's epic is docs authoring; the components it \"touches\" — its content describes serving/training, but the epic's work surface is the Documentation component. No context file covers Documentation. Score 0 with accurate rationale. Fine.\n\nE001/E002: Investigation epics with investigation_signals (not ai_signals) — correct type-appropriate fields. ✓ And no ai-signals contradictions.\n\nWait — E001 and E002 have ai-signals files (RHAISTRAT-9020-E001-ai-signals.md) but with the 5-signal investigation rubric. The prompt step 4 says read ai signal rationale files — fine, they exist and use the investigation rubric. ✓\n\nNow check investigation signal values against rubric conditions. Let me read the investigation rubric quickly to verify E001/E002 values.","signature":"3487793a7c904d00801e9cbdf946363a"}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":36575,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2a98fe0ecec4dd8","agent_id":"a984887860b9faab1","session_id":"ee31f95d-bee0-49c9-bebd-617d8f30fd03","uuid":"c8bbf4c5-227e-4fe0-abca-f3d9e3b2b30d","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:19:43.749Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
